---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy & Recruitment Compliance Notice | Init Source Ltd"
  description="How Init Source Ltd collects, uses, shares, stores, and protects recruitment data under UK data protection law."
  canonical="https://initsource.co.uk/privacy"
>
  <section id="privacy-policy" class="section bg-white">
    <div class="container maxw py-16 md:py-20 prose prose-neutral">
      <h1 class="h1 font-extrabold text-text">Privacy Policy & Recruitment Compliance Notice</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: October 2025</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Init Source Ltd is a UK-based recruitment company acting primarily as an
        Employment Agency for permanent recruitment and, where applicable, an
        Employment Business.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Company name:</strong> Init Source Ltd<br />
        <strong>Company number:</strong> 16785993<br />
        <strong>Registered office:</strong> 71-75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London, WC2H 9JQ, United Kingdom<br />
        <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@initsource.co.uk">contact@initsource.co.uk</a>
      </p>

      <h2>2. What personal data we collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect and process the following information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Name, email address, phone number, location, and other contact details</li>
        <li>CVs, work history, employment history, qualifications, skills, certifications, salary expectations, availability, notice period, and employment preferences</li>
        <li>Right-to-work and compliance information where required</li>
        <li>Interview notes, screening notes, client feedback, references, and communication history</li>
        <li>Information about roles, applications, interviews, offers, placements, and recruitment activity</li>
        <li>Information provided by candidates, clients, referees, job boards, LinkedIn, referrals, public professional sources, and other recruitment-related sources</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We only collect information that is relevant to recruitment, candidate representation,
        client hiring, compliance, or related business purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How we use your data</h2>
      <p>We use personal data to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Assess candidate suitability for Platform Engineering, SRE, DevOps, Cloud Infrastructure, and related roles</li>
        <li>Represent candidates to relevant employers for genuine recruitment opportunities</li>
        <li>Communicate about vacancies, interviews, feedback, offers, onboarding, and related recruitment activity</li>
        <li>Introduce suitable candidates to clients and suitable roles to candidates</li>
        <li>Manage client relationships, candidate relationships, recruitment processes, and placement records</li>
        <li>Verify information where appropriate, including references and right-to-work or compliance information</li>
        <li>Meet legal, regulatory, tax, accounting, and compliance obligations</li>
        <li>Keep records of recruitment activity, introductions, submissions, interviews, offers, and placements</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal data.</p>
      <p>
        We will not submit your CV or identifiable candidate profile to an employer without
        your prior knowledge and permission for that specific opportunity.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Lawful basis for processing</h2>
      <p>We process personal data under the following lawful bases in accordance with UK GDPR:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> for recruitment, candidate representation, client hiring support, business development, talent mapping, candidate sourcing, and placement activity</li>
        <li><strong>Consent:</strong> where consent is required, such as certain marketing communications or where we ask for permission to represent you for a specific role</li>
        <li><strong>Contract or pre-contract steps:</strong> where processing is necessary in relation to recruitment services, candidate representation, client engagement, or potential employment arrangements</li>
        <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> where processing is required for legal, regulatory, tax, accounting, right-to-work, or compliance purposes</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You may withdraw consent at any time where we rely on consent.</p>
      <p>
        Where we rely on legitimate interests, we do so only where we consider that our
        interests are not overridden by your rights, freedoms, or interests.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Special category and sensitive data</h2>
      <p>
        We do not intentionally collect special category data unless it is necessary for
        recruitment, right-to-work, reasonable adjustment, equality, legal, or compliance purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Special category data may include information relating to health, disability, ethnicity,
        religious beliefs, or other protected characteristics where relevant and lawfully processed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where special category data is processed, we will only do so where a valid UK GDPR
        condition applies and appropriate safeguards are in place.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not request criminal record information unless it is relevant and lawful for
        the role or required by the Client or applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>Where relevant and appropriate, we may share personal data with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Prospective employers and hiring organisations</li>
        <li>Client contacts involved in recruitment decisions</li>
        <li>Referees, where reference checks are required</li>
        <li>Compliance, legal, accounting, or professional advisers</li>
        <li>Technology providers used to store, manage, or process recruitment data</li>
        <li>Regulators, public authorities, or legal bodies where required by law</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Candidate data is shared only where relevant to genuine recruitment activity and, for
        CV submissions or identifiable candidate representation, with the candidate's prior
        knowledge and permission.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data storage, security, and retention</h2>
      <p>We store personal data in secure systems with access restricted to authorised personnel.</p>
      <p>
        We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data
        against unauthorised access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure.
      </p>
      <p>
        Candidate records are normally retained for up to 12 months from our last meaningful
        contact with you, unless a longer period is required for legal, contractual, accounting,
        compliance, or dispute-resolution purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Client and placement records may be retained for longer where necessary for contractual,
        legal, accounting, tax, compliance, or dispute-resolution purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want us to delete your data sooner, you can contact us at
        <a href="mailto:contact@initsource.co.uk">contact@initsource.co.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. International data transfers</h2>
      <p>We do not routinely transfer personal data outside the UK.</p>
      <p>
        Where international transfers are required, we will use appropriate safeguards such
        as the UK International Data Transfer Agreement, UK Addendum, Standard Contractual
        Clauses, or another lawful transfer mechanism.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Automated decision-making and AI tools</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use solely automated decision-making that produces legal or similarly
        significant effects.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where technology or AI-assisted tools are used to support recruitment administration,
        screening, drafting, search, or communication, human review remains part of the
        recruitment process. Final recruitment decisions are not made solely by automated systems.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Request access to your personal data</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
        <li>Request erasure of your personal data</li>
        <li>Request restriction of processing</li>
        <li>Object to processing</li>
        <li>Request data portability where applicable</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li>
        <li>Complain to the Information Commissioner's Office</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can make a request by contacting:
        <strong><a href="mailto:contact@initsource.co.uk">contact@initsource.co.uk</a></strong>
      </p>

      <h2>11. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you have concerns about how your data is handled, please contact us first at
        <a href="mailto:contact@initsource.co.uk">contact@initsource.co.uk</a> so we can
        try to resolve the issue.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the UK Information Commissioner's Office:
        <strong><a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary hover:underline">ico.org.uk</a></strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
